<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Asteroxylon mackiei Schnakenberg critical wavelength at 5.2 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 87.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the 5.2 µm, 407 Ma Schnakenberg calibration (δ = 160, 156 µm × 117 µm window, σ(k_c) = 0.3961, equal-diffusion σ_max = -0.0800). Activator contrast α is now the largest value whose Pearson r on the top 75% of rows stays at or above 0.985. That rule selects α = 0.35. Held-out bottom 25% scores r = 0.98639. Full-frame r = 0.98783, RMSE = 8.096 gray levels, gray-level KS = 0.161. The leafy-axis envelope on the model scale bar is 117 µm, against the 5.2 µm stripe; the spectral centroid of the activator is 7.646 µm. The δ sweep remains monotonic. Asteroxylon chronoseries is 1/1 at 407 Ma; the 283.4 µm enation sibling is 54.5 times longer and is not re-parameterized here. Overall 87.7/100 (faithfulness 87.6, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8f0e4833ae7c01aa84482096856ead2148c3f912; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8f0e4833ae7c01aa84482096856ead2148c3f912, image/png, 816591 B, 1344×960 px, artifact_sha256 fd44e2c72e7684d805d6919d20e45779d6d498602ffa1c6da45d662ccf945eee (sha256 fd44e2c72e7684d805d6919d20e45779d6d498602ffa1c6da45d662ccf945eee), spec_fingerprint 716e903fe3a6b195756b816d8895f02c8c7f83e58d092ed921cdf0ea6a927c85. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 716e903fe3a6b195756b816d8895f02c8c7f83e58d092ed921cdf0ea6a927c85; artifact_sha256: fd44e2c72e7684d805d6919d20e45779d6d498602ffa1c6da45d662ccf945eee; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=8d4cec453c791d09..., datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=9577842bd82c5dae..., datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=ad3ca375be91c9cf..., datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=345af56bd8c1eb6a..., datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=95e0c02c8d34e83a...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Kidston & Lang 1920: actinostele and microphyll leaf traces (DOI 10.1017/s0080456800004506). | Edwards, Kenrick & Dolan 2017: Rhynie Chert, Pragian, used here as 407 Ma. | Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics. | Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: short-range activation and long-range inhibition, the reason δ = 160 is large. | Hetherington et al. 2021: whole-plant reconstruction that this 156 µm window does not replace.; reconstructed_in_script: λ_c = 5.2 µm at δ = 160 on a 30-wavelength tracheid-file window. | α selected on the top 75% of rows; Pearson r reported on the bottom 25% (R1). | Two-sample KS between plate and render gray histograms (R2). | Axis-envelope wavelength 117 µm under the model scale bar, set beside 5.2 µm (R3). | Equal-diffusion ablation and the monotonic δ sweep, carried forward from Pass 1.; transfer_boundary: 117 µm envelope versus 5.2 µm stripe is the quantitative transfer gap. The Kenraiz plate is not a 5.2 µm micrograph. | Metres per pixel equal domain width divided by image height. That is a model scale bar.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured Asteroxylon pigment period of 5.2 µm in the Rhynie chert. | Does not claim the PDE generates the compression fossil from noise; the plate is the basic-look canvas. | Does not claim the 283 µm sibling's diffusivities. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. Signing was skipped because ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Closed in Pass 2. α = 0.35 chosen on the top 75% of rows; bottom 25% Pearson r = 0.98639.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Closed in Pass 2. Gray-level KS = 0.161 against reference 0.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Closed in Pass 2. Leafy-axis envelope = 117 µm against the 5.2 µm stripe.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.77e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

