<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Asteroxylon mackiei Schnakenberg critical wavelength at 5.2 µm (Pass 2) (Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid))",
        "Asteroxylon mackiei Schnakenberg critical wavelength at 5.2 µm (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured Asteroxylon pigment period of 5.2 µm in the Rhynie chert.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a signed nanopublication. Signing was skipped because ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the 283 µm sibling's diffusivities.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the PDE generates the compression fossil from noise; the plate is the basic-look canvas.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Axis-envelope wavelength 117 µm under the model scale bar, set beside 5.2 µm (R3).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Equal-diffusion ablation and the monotonic δ sweep, carried forward from Pass 1.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Two-sample KS between plate and render gray histograms (R2).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: α selected on the top 75% of rows; Pearson r reported on the bottom 25% (R1).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: λ_c = 5.2 µm at δ = 160 on a 30-wavelength tracheid-file window.",
        "reported_in_source: Edwards, Kenrick & Dolan 2017: Rhynie Chert, Pragian, used here as 407 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: short-range activation and long-range inhibition, the reason δ = 160 is large.",
        "reported_in_source: Hetherington et al. 2021: whole-plant reconstruction that this 156 µm window does not replace.",
        "reported_in_source: Kidston & Lang 1920: actinostele and microphyll leaf traces (DOI 10.1017/s0080456800004506).",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics.",
        "transfer_boundary: 117 µm envelope versus 5.2 µm stripe is the quantitative transfer gap. The Kenraiz plate is not a 5.2 µm micrograph.",
        "transfer_boundary: Metres per pixel equal domain width divided by image height. That is a model scale bar." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian (Pragian Rhynie Chert, 407 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Asteroxylon" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Kidston & Lang 1920: actinostele and microphyll leaf traces (DOI 10.1017/s0080456800004506). | Edwards, Kenrick & Dolan 2017: Rhynie Chert, Pragian, used here as 407 Ma. | Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics. | Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: short-range activation and long-range inhibition, the reason δ = 160 is large. | Hetherington et al. 2021: whole-plant reconstruction that this 156 µm window does not replace.; reconstructed_in_script: λ_c = 5.2 µm at δ = 160 on a 30-wavelength tracheid-file window. | α selected on the top 75% of rows; Pearson r reported on the bottom 25% (R1). | Two-sample KS between plate and render gray histograms (R2). | Axis-envelope wavelength 117 µm under the model scale bar, set beside 5.2 µm (R3). | Equal-diffusion ablation and the monotonic δ sweep, carried forward from Pass 1.; transfer_boundary: 117 µm envelope versus 5.2 µm stripe is the quantitative transfer gap. The Kenraiz plate is not a 5.2 µm micrograph. | Metres per pixel equal domain width divided by image height. That is a model scale bar.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured Asteroxylon pigment period of 5.2 µm in the Rhynie chert. | Does not claim the PDE generates the compression fossil from noise; the plate is the basic-look canvas. | Does not claim the 283 µm sibling's diffusivities. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. Signing was skipped because ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent.]; phenomenon_size: 5.7 µm (5.668e-06 m, log10=-5.247 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 5.7 µm to 1.3 cm): 5.7 µm:asteroxylon-mackiei-bioelectric-polarity, 18 µm:asteroxylon-mackiei-vertex-packing, 283 µm:asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength, 567 µm:asteroxylon-mackiei-clock-wavefront, 1.3 mm:asteroxylon-mackiei-morphogen-condensation, 1.6 mm:asteroxylon-mackiei-elastic-buckling, 1.8 mm:asteroxylon-mackiei-flux-canalization, 2.5 mm:asteroxylon-mackiei-branching-tree" ;
